35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found that our advisers are sitting on the bench. We have the people, but we’re not using them.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,George,,I looked at the exits. The ones that made money were boring back-office tools. The one that failed was a physical shop.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"I checked the reserves. We are bleeding cash on follow-ons. And the credit line only likes physical stock, not software.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,I found that hardware needs outside appraisals. That adds six weeks to our quarter-end. I can’t do that again.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,I found that security reviews take three quarters for regulated customers. And the hardware deal lost five months to a chip shortage.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, so the boring tools are the winners? That means we don’t need to build a factory, just a team.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,George,,Exactly. The back-office tools kept their customers even when they raised prices. The physical one lost a third.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Mizuki, if the hardware takes three quarters to deploy, we can’t borrow against it. It’s dead money for us.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@May, that’s why I’m worried. If we can’t verify the numbers, we can’t report them. I need a company that reports itself.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, I agree. The software tool never missed a release. It’s predictable. The hardware is a black hole.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"So we need a software company that doesn’t need a factory. That way, I can use my advisers to find the team.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,George,,"And it needs to be a tool that people can’t live without. If they raise prices, the customers stay.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"And it needs to be something we can borrow against. If it’s just code, we can’t. But if it’s a service, maybe.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,"And it needs to be something I can verify. If it’s a dashboard, I can check the numbers myself. No outside appraisals.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"And it needs to be something that deploys fast. If it’s a plugin, it’s in the system in a week. Not a quarter.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I think we’re all pointing to the same thing. A software tool that is essential, predictable, and easy to verify.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,George,,"I’m with you. I’ve seen enough of the physical mess. I want the boring, reliable software.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"I’m with you. I need to know if we can afford the next round. If it’s a service, we can model the cash flow.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I’m with you. I need to close the books in two weeks, not six. I need a company that reports itself.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"I’m with you. I need to know that the money reaches the customer. If it’s a plugin, it’s live in a week.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
